      "content": "Religious conservatives generally argue that medical aid in dying undermines the sanctity of human life, goes against Cardinal Joseph Ratzinger's definition of euthanasia, and can lead to abuse of vulnerable individuals. They often cite scriptures and teachings, such as the 6th Commandment, to justify their position that all human life must be protected. In contrast, religious liberals emphasize the importance of compassion, autonomy, and compassionately ending suffering. They also point to the character of Jesus as a model for loving and caring for those in pain, yet respecting their free will. While there are variations within each group, this is a general outline of their moral arguments.",
